assistant: Subject: Read unit_amount when vendor omits price

Vendor API version 2026-10-01 no longer sends `price` and puts the unit price in `unit_amount` instead, so `get_product` turned the missing field into `price: null`. I changed `get_product` to fall back to `unit_amount` when `price` is missing (`p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`). I didn't convert the value: in the recordings, v1 `price` and v2 `unit_amount` are both 1199 for p-1001, so they use the same dollar units. I made the same fallback in `search_products`, which reads `price` the same way. No recording shows search failing, so that part is a precaution. Old-version responses still include `price`, so the v1 fixtures give exactly the same output. Typecheck, lint and all 14 tests pass, including the repro test.

